      "published": "2026-07-25T11:33:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "The POSIX shell `:` built-in evaluates arguments without execution, enabling variable default assignments like `: \"${VAR:=default}\"`.",
        "It serves as a zero-overhead no-op placeholder for required shell syntax blocks, such as empty `if` branches or `while :` loops.",
        "Combining `:` with redirections (`: > file`) portably truncates files while explicitly signaling intentional code execution."
      ]
